    offer_curve_by_group: { cell: "U", ev: "SOCO-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/soco-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SOCO-21) — U: UNTESTED, and deliberately NOT `.`. Gate G5: the rule 1 [R-STRUCT] / rule 13 [R-MEASURED] carve-out authorizes tuning MARKET OFFERS and SOCO takes none — its dispatch is cost-based — so the desk's posture is that SOCO's bands STAY 1.0 unless the owner rules otherwise, and a SOCO band != 1.0 needs a much stronger story than an RTO's (a non-neutral band in the generic fallback would also breach rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]). What that closes is the AUTHORIZED PRICE-TUNING CHANNEL, not the row's own object: SOCO's first keeper will carry per-class band curves (at neutral 1.0), and the duty-role cohort splits and econ-ramp shape anchor registered on this row under rule 28(c) are live SOCO questions. `.` would claim there is no SOCO object, which is false, so this cell reads U with the channel closed on the record. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.8." },
